# Writing documentation

@@name@@'s documentation is one tree of plain Markdown under `docs/`, and every way of reading it is a
rendering of that tree: the site at `@@site_url@@`, `llms.txt`, `llms-full.txt`, a Markdown copy of
each page, `docs-index.json`, and the agent skill in the plugin under `marketplace/plugins/@@name@@/`.
The tool that checks and renders it is ankka's documentation tool, and so are the rules:
[Documentation rules](https://docs.ankka.cloud/reference/documentation-rules/) states every rule a page
follows, with its reason. This page says what is particular to this repository.

## The build

```bash
uv run --project tools/docs docs check    # every rule; exits 1 on a problem
uv run --project tools/docs docs sync     # refresh included samples, generated blocks and the skill
uv run --project tools/docs docs build    # check, build the site, write the machine renderings
uv run --project tools/docs docs serve    # the site with live reload, while writing
uv run --project tools/docs docs init     # write the kept parts again, and any part that is missing
```

The site lands in `target/docs-site`. What the tool needs to know about this repository is
`extra.docs` in `mkdocs.yml`.

## The parts the tool keeps

Two files are the documentation tool's, not this repository's: `tools/docs/pyproject.toml`, which names
the release of the tool that builds this documentation, and `.github/workflows/docs.yml`, which checks
the documentation on every pull request and publishes the site to GitHub Pages when a release is
tagged. The first tag publishes only once the repository's `github-pages` environment lets tags named
`v*` deploy (Settings, Environments), which GitHub does not allow until told.

`docs check` fails when either file differs from what that release of the tool writes, and `docs init`
writes both again. A later release of the tool is taken by running `docs init` from it, which rewrites
both files and leaves every file this repository owns as it is:

```bash
uvx --from "git+https://github.com/thinkmorestupidless/ankka@v<release>#subdirectory=tools/docs" docs init
```

## Where a page goes

| Kind | Directory | The reader wants to |
|---|---|---|
| `tutorial` | `get-started/` | be walked from nothing to something working |
| `concept` | `concepts/` | understand how something works and why |
| `guide` | `build/`, `deploy/` | get one task done |
| `reference` | `reference/` | look one fact up |
| `contributing` | `contributing/` | change @@name@@ itself |

A new page is added to the `nav` in `mkdocs.yml` and, unless it is a contributing page, to the
`pages:` list of the skill in `tools/docs/skill/@@name@@/SKILL.md`, or the check fails.
